        "elder_staff",
        "vigil_mace",
        "studded_wraps",
        "wold_cloth_hood",
        "wold_cloth_robe",
        "wold_cloth_slops",
        "wold_cloth_shoes",
        "lampright_cap",
        "lampright_vest",
        "lampright_trews",
        "lampright_boots",
        "thornguard_coif",
        "thornguard_hauberk",
        "thornguard_chausses",
        "thornguard_sabatons",
        "waywatcher_hood",
        "waywatcher_jerkin",
        "waywatcher_trews",
        "waywatcher_boots",
        "argent_cap",
        "argent_robe",
        "argent_slops",
        "argent_shoes",
        "greywall_helm",
        "greywall_hauberk",
        "greywall_chausses",
        "greywall_sabatons"
      ],
      "dialog": [
        "Swords for the shield line, katanas for the duelling code, and chain for anyone who means to be hit and remain upright.",
        "Three hundred years of drill and not one sword drawn in anger. The steel doesn't know that. Keep it oiled.",
        "The court buys the garrison's kit from me on credit against the day the empire pays. I have a very long ledger and a very patient wife.",
        "Robes. Staves. Wraps for people who punch things for a living. The court says every job buys at its own city's door now, so here they hang, between my good swords. Don't touch the chain with ink on your hands."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "chandler_mott",
      "name": "Chandler Mott",
      "kind": "vendor",
      "title": "The Market Crossroads",
      "stock": [
        "potion",
        "hi_potion",
        "ether",
        "antidote",
        "eye_drops",
        "remedy",
        "traveler_tunic",
        "traveler_slops",
        "traveler_boots",
        "traveler_hood",
        "hi_ether"
      ],
      "dialog": [
        "Potions, salves, a coat that keeps the fjord out. If the wall wants it, I stock it; if the wall doesn't want it, someone's cousin does.",
        "Fish carts yield for no one. You'll learn."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "broker_ashby",
      "name": "Broker Ashby",
      "kind": "auction",
      "title": "The Auction House",
      "dialog": [
        "The auction house of Caerdun, chartered by the court, three percent to the treasury and not a copper more, whatever Moonmere charges.",
        "Relics sell here. Relics also register with the court, for standing rather than gold. The court remembers who did which."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "drillmaster_hal",
      "name": "Drillmaster Hal",
      "kind": "sanctuary",
      "title": "The Paladin Hall",
      "dialog": [
        "Shield line to the north hall, duelling code to the south, and the parade square between them where the two argue about which of them is Caerdun.",
        "Every job is open to an explorer. Stand in the hall's light to take up another; the body remembers what the drill taught it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "innkeeper_sayre",
      "name": "Innkeeper Sayre",
      "kind": "vendor",
      "title": "The Crown Inn",
      "stock": [
        "potion",
        "hi_potion",
        "ether",
        "lantern_oil_flask"
      ],
      "dialog": [
        "A bed, a bowl, and a fire that has not gone out since the Sealing. My family has a bet on with the wall about which lasts longer.",
        "Envoys, freebooters, sergeants off shift. Everybody's somebody's story in here."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "guildmaster_torv",
      "name": "Guildmaster Torv",
      "kind": "flavor",
      "title": "The Smiths' Guild",
      "dialog": [
        "Iron from the Fields' seams, shell from the fen, antler from the wood. Bring me the makings and the guild will teach you the making. Press K to see what your hands know.",
        "The empire's blades were better than ours. The empire's blades are also three hundred years away. Ours are here."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "quartermaster_kettle",
      "name": "Quartermaster Ingrid Kettle",
      "kind": "vendor",
      "title": "The Halls' Stores",
      "stock": [
        "calling_pld_14_head",
        "calling_sam_14_head"
      ],
      "dialog": [
        "The halls' stores. Helms for the shield line, headguards for the duelling code, each one entered in the hall's account under your name. Boots are the doorstep's business.",
        "The hall's account, your name, paid in full or not at all. The court has run on credit for three hundred years; my shelf does not.",
        "Wear it when your job has earned the level. I sell early. The steel can wait for you; it has had practice."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "shield_captain_lund",
      "name": "Shield-Captain Thora Lund",
      "kind": "quest",
      "title": "The Shield Line",
      "dialog": [
        "The shield line's terms are short. Hold until relieved. Three hundred years on, I can give you the shift count to the day; my father Bertil kept the tally before me and keeps it yet, retired, at the kitchen table.",
        "A recruit's days of service are wages owed. I keep the hall's roll; Vail's vault gets the copy, and the empire can argue the rate when it gets home.",
        "Paladin work is given out of this hall. Not by Hal; Hal teaches the body. I teach the terms."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "code_master_rudd",
      "name": "Code-Master Eskil Rudd",
      "kind": "quest",
      "title": "The Duelling Code",
      "h": -1.5708,
      "dialog": [
        "The code is three pages. The commentary is four hundred. Sabel keeps the commentary and the yard; I keep the three pages and the hall.",
        "A duel is a contract with a witness. Everything else that happens with a sword is weather.",
        "My cousin grinds blades on Smiths' Lane. She says nobody brings her a dull one twice. That is the whole curriculum."
      ]
    }
  ],
